{
  "_id": "tg-vanity",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "they have provoked me to anger with their vanities, Deut. 32:21. they followed vanity, and became vain, 2 Kgs. 17:15. Let not him that is deceived trust in vanity, Job 15:31. how long will ye love vanity, Ps. 4:2. They speak vanity every one with his neighbour, Ps. 12:2. who hath not lifted up his soul unto vanity, Ps. 24:4. I have hated them that regard lying vanities, Ps. 31:6. every man at his best state is altogether vanity, Ps. 39:5. their days did he consume in vanity, Ps. 78:33. knoweth the thoughts of man, that they are vanity, Ps. 94:11. strange children, whose mouth speaketh vanity, Ps. 144:11. Wealth gotten by vanity shall be diminished, Prov. 13:11. getting of treasures by a lying tongue is a vanity, Prov. 21:6. Vanity of vanities, saith the Preacher, Eccl. 1:2 (12:8). all is vanity and vexation of spirit, Eccl. 1:14 (2:11, 17, 26; 6:9). hath not laboured … This also is vanity, Eccl. 2:21. I saw vanity under the sun, Eccl. 4:7. in the multitude of dreams and many words there are also divers vanities, Eccl. 5:7. loveth silver … abundance … this is also vanity, Eccl. 5:10. laughter of the fool: this also is vanity, Eccl. 7:6. All things have I seen in the days of my vanity, Eccl. 7:15. draw iniquity with cords of vanity, Isa. 5:18 (2 Ne. 15:18). sift the nations with the sieve of vanity, Isa. 30:28. nations … counted … less than nothing, and vanity, Isa. 40:17 (41:29). they trust in vanity, Isa. 59:4. they … have walked after vanity, Jer. 2:5. They are vanity, and the work of errors, Jer. 10:15 (51:18). our fathers have inherited lies, vanity, Jer. 16:19. They have seen vanity and lying divination, Ezek. 13:6. shall weary themselves for very vanity, Hab. 2:13.",
